# How buerligons reaches a ClassCAD engine. The first configured option wins, in this order:
#
# 1. WSCLIENT_URL   - Drogon multi-client server (session sharing + invite panel). The share
#                     panel appears for the host, i.e. a session opened without ?invite=.
#                     `yarn dev:cli` sets it via .env.cli.
# 2. CLASSCAD_TOKEN - ClassCAD engine in the browser (WASM), unlocked with a *public* access
#                     token (ccpk_...) from https://classcad.ch/account. The token may sit in a
#                     web page and works on localhost and on the domains registered in the account.
#                     The client exchanges it for a short-lived engine key and renews that key by
#                     itself, so there is no expiry date to maintain. Never put a secret token
#                     (ccsk_...) here.
# 3. SOCKETIO_URL   - SocketIO connection to a local or remote ClassCAD server (the default).
#
# Keep personal values out of git: put them into an untracked .env.local, which Vite loads on
# top of this file.

# WSCLIENT_URL=ws://localhost:9094
# CLASSCAD_TOKEN=ccpk_<your-public-access-token-goes-here>
SOCKETIO_URL=ws://localhost:9091

# Collaboration features (peer cameras, follow mode, cursors) are always on in
# shared sessions - no configuration needed or possible here.
